abstract: >-
  RUSCUAV is a benchmark for low-altitude urban cargo-UAV navigation that scores
  missions by semantic mission acceptability (cargo health, time over roads,
  pedestrian ways, buildings and sensitive zones, hard violations) as well as by
  target-reaching success. The ruscuav-benchmark package provides validated world
  files, a Gymnasium environment, the risk-cost A* planners and PPO policies of the
  paper, evaluation protocols with fixed missions, scoring of any method's
  trajectories, the paper's statistics, and a builder of worlds from OpenStreetMap
  data. The code is MIT-licensed; data, worlds and documentation are CC BY 4.0.
